  "fixed_text": {
    "bumpy": "Volatility measures how widely returns swung around their average, up as well as down. It describes the past, not the future.",
    "worst": "Falls are measured from one month-end to the next, so a fall that recovered within a month doesn't show. The £10,000 figure applies only to money invested at the high.",
